From 36a82f93511a906c579a3d5100eb00e98493d0cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:27:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Give Baidu and Niutrans a dedicated App ID field

The two new engines kept both credentials joined as "appid#secret"
in the single API key field, which failed in practice: switching
from another engine left the old key in place (shown as "set" while
every request failed the usability check), the format hint only
appeared while the field was empty, and Niutrans users had nowhere
to learn that an App ID was expected at all.

Profiles now carry a real appId field next to the API key: the
settings show a dedicated "App ID" input for the two engines, the
usability check and the master-switch summary name the exact field
that is missing, and the connection-test failure message does too.
Switching the engine clears the credentials, since they never carry
over and a stale key only reads as configured. Profiles stored with
the old joined format are migrated automatically on load.

The engines read the two fields directly; the compound-key splitter
is gone.
